pe":"text","text":" invoked when the task is canceled. For example, even if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operation is running code that never checks for cancellation, a cancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler still runs and provides a chance to run some cleanup code:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["await withTaskCancellationHandler {","  var sum = 0","  while condition {","    sum += 1","  }","  return sum","} onCancel: { reason in","  \/\/ This onCancel closure might execute concurrently with the operation.","  condition.cancel()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Execution order and semantics","anchor":"Execution-order-and-semantics","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure is always invoked, even when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method is called from a task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that was already canceled."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is used in a task that has already been","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"canceled, the cancellation handler will be executed","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"immediately before the ","type":"text"},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure gets to execute.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This allows the cancellation handler to set some external “canceled” flag"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that the operation may be ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"atomically"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" checking for in order to avoid","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"performing any actual work once the operation gets to run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operation"},{"type":"text","text":" closure executes on the calling execution context, and doesn’t"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"suspend or change execution context unless code contained within the closure"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does so. In other words, the potential suspension point of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler(operation:onCancel:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" never suspends by itself before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"executing the operation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If cancellation occurs while the operation is running, the cancellation","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler executes "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"concurrently"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" with the operation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The reason passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handler"},{"text":" is the same value that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.cancellationReason"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would report on the task being cancelled. However, the handler is invoked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"cancelling","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" context, not from the cancelled task’s own context,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"so checking ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.cancellationReason"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside the "},{"code":"onCancel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would report the cancellation status of the cancelling context rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that of the task being cancelled; use the passed-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reason"},{"text":" parameter,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which does represent the cancelled task’s status."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancellation handlers and locks","anchor":"Cancellation-handlers-and-locks","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancellation handlers which acquire locks must take care to avoid deadlock."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The cancellation handler may be invoked while holding internal locks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"associated with the task or other tasks.  Other operations on the task, such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as resuming a continuation, may acquire these same internal locks.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Therefore, if a cancellation handler must acquire a lock, other code should","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not cancel tasks or resume continuations while holding that lock.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Execute an operation with a cancellation handler that’s immediately","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"invoked with the cancellation reason when the current task is canceled.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/isCancelled-swift.type.property","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/cancel()","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/cancel(reason:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/cancellationReason","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Task\/checkCancellation()","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CancellationError","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CancellationError\/Reason-swift.enum","doc: